PRETABLE 15a -- #529 crimewidthkill, the pass-2 candidate against REPAIR 15.  Written 2026-09-26 BEFORE any build or
probe run of this table; this file's mtime is the order proof and it is never edited after the table starts
(corrections go to POSTTABLE15a.out).

WHY.  The dedicated adversarial grok seat on repair 15's pass 2 (repair15_pass2_20260926/grok_dedicated_r15p2.txt,
"BREAK FOUND") named an edit it reasons the 218 rows cannot see: delete `idata &= ~CRIME_CONTROL_HARD_RESET;' in the
CONTROL arm's HARD_RESET branch.  An escape is a MEASUREMENT, never an inference, so it is measured here before the
F2 packet grades it.  Reading the arm for the CLASS gave a sibling: the arm has exactly three clears -- DOG (the
branch at dev_sgi_ip32.c 8c1d1545 :361-363, rowed by repair 15's ctldog pair), HARD_RESET (:364-373, the grok
candidate) and ENDIANESS (:375, unconditional) -- and each is visible only through the residue print at :377-379.
E_noendianclear is the third.

INSTRUMENT: the table-14 probe, crime_width_probe.table14.py f5e915f6, UNCHANGED (218 rows).  BASELINE: the working
tree, dev_sgi_ip32.c 8c1d1545, the same bytes and the same clone (/tmp/gxopus_r14) as table 14, whose base leg read
218/218 at 00:54 (table14_20260926/logs/probe_base.raw).  No base leg is re-run here: the probe, the source and the
clone are those of table 14, and the driver re-checks all three (md5 and cmp) before mutant 1.
MUTATOR: mutants_15a.py a614547c (dry-run before this file: each a single deleted line; `base' byte-identical).

PREDICTIONS -- both ESCAPE, exact:
  H_noresetclear   218/218, FAILING none, CRIMEP_CONTROL OK.
    Every session with an accepted 0x800 write -- `sw08 halts' (sw, latch clear), `rst 4w' / `rst 8w' (sw / sd, latch
    set by a leading `lb +0x07') -- reads the CPU STOP only (v1 left at the sentinel), and the stop still happens: the
    loop that clears `running' precedes the deleted clear.  None counts `CRIME_CONTROL: unimplemented'.  The rows
    that do count that text write no 0x800: `sw08 msg ctl' (0x01), `acc ctl sd' (0x01), `p acc ctl msg' (0x01, 0x0001,
    0x0201, 0x0201), `ctldog sw/sd msg' (0x0200, 0x0201), and `sb08 msg' / `sh08b msg' are REFUSED narrow writes that
    never reach the arm.  `rst 4w once' / `rst 8w once' count `-- declined.', which the new text does not contain.
  E_noendianclear  218/218, FAILING none, CRIMEP_CONTROL OK.
    The only ACCEPTED CONTROL writes carrying 0x100 are ACCEPTS's two ENDIANESS entries (sw and sd 0x0100), in the
    `rearm' and `latch x5' sessions, whose rows count `-- declined.' and a RAM trip -- never the CONTROL text.  No
    other accepted CONTROL write sets 0x100 (sh08b's 0x0900 is a REFUSED 2-byte write, declined before the arm).

SCORING: check15a.py beside this file.  A predicted escape that DOES red a row is recorded as a miss with the rows
named -- it would mean the cell was carried after all, and the owed rows shrink accordingly.

WHAT FOLLOWS IF BOTH ESCAPE (for the F2 packet and the adjudicators, not decided here): the ruling's 13/17 conditional
("if a body-tested-partition mutant escapes -> L2, IN as the pair") applies to H_noresetclear on its own words --
HARD_RESET is a TESTED bit of the arm.  ENDIANESS is not tested (cleared unconditionally, never branched on), so by
the pinned meaning of "tests" it is outside the generating set; whether its residue cell is floor or clause (e) is a
RULE QUESTION for the adjudicators.  And it is the SECOND consecutive pass finding a residue-of-a-clear cell in one arm
(repair 14's adjudication found DOG; this pass found HARD_RESET), which is the repair-chain amendment's trigger for a
CLASS CLOSURE of all three clears in one diff.
